{# ============================================================================
   THE REPORT FLOW — ONE component, mounted over whichever surface you were on.

   Filing an incident must not feel like five different products just because five
   dashboards can lead to it, so the dashboard's sheet and the dedicated page at
   /areas/{uuid}/modules/incidents/new are THIS FILE, twice.

   STEP 2 IS THE CATEGORY'S OWN. Every sub-category's field set is rendered and
   all but the chosen one are hidden AND disabled, so the posted form carries only
   the fields the chosen kind of incident actually asks for. The MONEY row exists
   only inside the field sets of categories that carry money — choose a natural
   mortality and there is no money row in the document at all. Not disabled.
   Absent.

   IT WORKS WITHOUT JAVASCRIPT: the sheet is `open` on its own page, the category
   is a radio, and the form posts normally. The Stimulus controller adds opening
   it over a dashboard and swapping the field set without a round trip.

   Parameters: area, categories, prefill, chosen, csrfToken, errors, standalone
   → POST /areas/{uuid}/modules/incidents
   ========================================================================== #}
{# THE CONTROLLER, NAMED ONCE. A controller shipped by a bundle is registered
   under its PACKAGE-QUALIFIED identifier, so every target and action has to be
   written through the stimulus_* helpers with that same name — a hand-written
   `incident-report#choose` is silently inert in a host app. #}
{% set controller = '@uhifadhilabs/incident-module/incident-report' %}
<div class="i-sheetbd{{ standalone ? ' open' }}"
     {{ stimulus_target(controller, 'sheet')|stimulus_action(controller, 'closeOnBackdrop', 'click') }}>
    {# input and change both bubble, so ONE action on the form re-reads the gate
       whatever the filer typed into. #}
    <form class="i-sheet" method="post" action="{{ path('incident_create', {uuid: area.uuid}) }}"
          {{ stimulus_action(controller, 'gate', 'input')|stimulus_action(controller, 'gate', 'change') }}>
        <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}">
        {# The provenance travels with the form, so whatever the filer changes on
           the way through, the record it came from is the record it came from. #}
        {% if prefill.record %}
            <input type="hidden" name="record" value="{{ prefill.record }}">
            <input type="hidden" name="label" value="{{ prefill.label }}">
            <input type="hidden" name="back" value="{{ prefill.backUrl }}">
            <input type="hidden" name="source" value="{{ prefill.source ?? 'patrol_observation' }}">
        {% endif %}

        <div class="i-sheethd">
            <div>
                <h2>Report an incident</h2>
                <p>Three steps. What kind and what happened are needed to file; who was involved can follow afterwards —
                    and the money fields appear only if the category you pick carries them.</p>
            </div>
            {% if not standalone %}
                <button class="x" type="button" {{ stimulus_action(controller, 'close') }} aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
            {% endif %}
        </div>

        {# THE SOURCE CARD. "How is the filing user going to remember the context
           of what happened?" By looking at it: the record this filing came from
           is pinned above the steps with its own words, its position in the same
           notation the observation page prints, its time and its photographs.
           Nothing on it is editable — provenance is written once, at filing. #}
        {% if prefill.hasProvenance %}
            <section class="i-src" data-incident-source-card>
                <div class="hd">{{ ux_icon('lucide:git-branch') }}<b>Filed from {{ prefill.label }}</b>
                    {% if prefill.backUrl %}<a class="go" href="{{ prefill.backUrl }}">Open the source →</a>{% endif %}</div>
                {% if prefill.note %}<p class="note">“{{ prefill.note }}”</p>{% endif %}
                <div class="facts">
                    {# `false` KEEPS THE MOMENT'S OWN ZONE. The observation was made
                       at 08:15 where the observer was standing, and a card meant to
                       be recognised must not restate it in UTC. #}
                    {% if prefill.occurredAt %}<span><em>when</em><b>{{ prefill.occurredAt|date('D j M Y · H:i', false)|lower }}</b></span>{% endif %}
                    {% if prefill.positionLabel %}<span><em>where</em><b>{{ prefill.positionLabel }}</b></span>{% endif %}
                    <span><em>source</em><b>{{ prefill.sourceLabel }}</b></span>
                </div>
                {# NO THUMBNAILS YET, and the reason is a missing seam, not an
                   oversight. The design draws the source record's photographs on
                   this card (.i-src .shots, in incidents.css, ported and waiting).
                   What arrives here is a record UUID and a source token, and
                   storage-module addresses files by KEY or by owner label only:
                   FileSourceInterface has files(), claimsKey(), guard() — no
                   filesForRecord(), and FileEntry carries no record uuid. The
                   only way to bridge that today is to walk FileRegistry::all()
                   and string-match the observation UUID inside another module's
                   ownerUrl, which is both a whole-deployment scan and a guess at
                   the patrols module's routing. Neither belongs in a bundle that
                   may be installed without patrols at all.
                   The seam this needs, in storage-module:
                     FileSourceInterface::filesForRecord(string $source, string $recordUuid): iterable<FileEntry>
                     FileRegistry::forRecord(string $source, string $recordUuid): list<FileEntry>
                   matched on moduleSlug(), with the source token the query string
                   already carries. Then this block is a loop over that list and
                   an <img src="{{ path('storage_evidence_show', {key: file.thumbKey}) }}">. #}
                <p class="seam">its category guess, coordinates, time and note are already in the form below · the link is
                    kept forever</p>
            </section>
        {% endif %}

        {% if errors is not empty %}
            <div class="i-errors">{% for error in errors %}<p>{{ error }}</p>{% endfor %}</div>
        {% endif %}

        <div class="i-steps"><span class="on">1 · category</span><span class="arr">→</span><span>2 · what happened</span><span class="arr">→</span><span>3 · people &amp; evidence</span></div>

        {# STEP 1 — what kind. Choosing one selects its first sub-category; step 2
           then offers the siblings, exactly as the design draws it. #}
        <div class="i-catpick">
            {% for category in categories %}
                {% set slugs = [] %}
                {% for sub in category.subcategories %}{% set slugs = slugs|merge([sub.slug]) %}{% endfor %}
                <label class="i-catopt{{ chosen and chosen.category.slug == category.slug ? ' on' }}"
                       {{ stimulus_target(controller, 'category')|stimulus_action(controller, 'choose', 'click') }}
                       data-subcategory="{{ slugs|first }}"
                       data-subcategories="{{ slugs|join(',') }}">
                    <span class="r"><i class="i-hue-{{ category.colourKey }}"></i><b>{{ category.label }}</b></span>
                    <span class="d">{% for sub in category.subcategories %}{{ sub.label }}{{ not loop.last ? ' · ' }}{% endfor %}</span>
                </label>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>

        {# STEP 2 — THE CATEGORY'S OWN FIELDS, one set per sub-category. #}
        {% for category in categories %}
            {% for subcategory in category.subcategories %}
                {% set isChosen = chosen and chosen.slug == subcategory.slug %}
                <div class="i-fieldset i-step2" {{ stimulus_target(controller, 'fieldset') }}
                     data-subcategory="{{ subcategory.slug }}"{{ isChosen ? '' : ' hidden' }}>
                    <div class="hd">Step 2 — the fields {{ subcategory.label }} asks for</div>

                    {# The siblings under this kind. Choosing one swaps the whole
                       field set, because the sub-category is what decides the
                       questions — and whether there is a money row at all. #}
                    <div class="i-fld"><label>Sub-category</label>
                        <span><span class="i-taxsub">
                            {%- for sibling in category.subcategories -%}
                                <a href="#" class="{{ sibling.slug == subcategory.slug ? 'on' }}"
                                   {{ stimulus_target(controller, 'category')|stimulus_action(controller, 'choose', 'click') }}
                                   data-subcategory="{{ sibling.slug }}"
                                   data-subcategories="{{ sibling.slug }}">{{ sibling.label }}</a>
                            {%- endfor -%}
                        </span></span></div>

                    <div class="i-fld"><label for="title-{{ subcategory.slug }}">What happened</label>
                        <span><input type="text" id="title-{{ subcategory.slug }}" name="title" maxlength="200"
                                     placeholder="One line — the register prints it"{{ isChosen ? '' : ' disabled' }}></span></div>
                    <div class="i-fld"><label for="when-{{ subcategory.slug }}">When</label>
                        <span><input type="datetime-local" id="when-{{ subcategory.slug }}" name="occurred_at"
                                     value="{{ prefill.occurredAt ? prefill.occurredAt|date('Y-m-d\\TH:i', false) }}"{{ isChosen ? '' : ' disabled' }}></span></div>
                    <div class="i-fld"><label>Where</label>
                        <span><input type="text" name="lat" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="latitude"
                                     value="{{ prefill.latitude }}"{{ isChosen ? '' : ' disabled' }}>
                              <input type="text" name="lng" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="longitude"
                                     value="{{ prefill.longitude }}"{{ isChosen ? '' : ' disabled' }}></span></div>
                    <div class="i-fld"><label for="sev-{{ subcategory.slug }}">Severity</label>
                        <span><select id="sev-{{ subcategory.slug }}" name="severity"{{ isChosen ? '' : ' disabled' }}>
                            <option value="low">low</option>
                            <option value="medium" selected>medium</option>
                            <option value="high">high</option>
                        </select></span></div>
                    <div class="i-fld"><label for="narr-{{ subcategory.slug }}">In their own words</label>
                        <span><textarea id="narr-{{ subcategory.slug }}" name="narrative" rows="3"
                                        placeholder="Verbatim — kept apart from the officer's assessment"{{ isChosen ? '' : ' disabled' }}>{{ prefill.note }}</textarea></span></div>

                    {% for field in subcategory.fieldSet %}
                        <div class="i-fld"><label for="d-{{ subcategory.slug }}-{{ field.key }}">{{ field.label }}</label>
                            <span><input type="text" id="d-{{ subcategory.slug }}-{{ field.key }}"
                                         name="details_{{ field.key }}"{{ isChosen ? '' : ' disabled' }}></span></div>
                    {% endfor %}

                    {# ONLY where this kind of incident carries money. #}
                    {% if subcategory.carriesMoney %}
                        <div class="i-fld only"><label>{{ subcategory.moneyDirection.value == 'fine' ? 'Fine to assess' : 'Loss claimed' }}</label>
                            <span class="i-kpi-note">Recorded on the case file once somebody has assessed it — filing is
                                cheap, and a figure guessed at the roadside is worse than none.</span></div>
                    {% endif %}
                </div>
            {% endfor %}
        {% endfor %}

        {# The chosen sub-category, as one value. The picker writes into it; without
           JavaScript the radios below carry it. #}
        <input type="hidden" name="subcategory" value="{{ chosen ? chosen.slug }}" data-incident-report-subcategory>
        <noscript>
            <div class="i-fieldset">
                <div class="hd">Step 1 — what kind of incident</div>
                {% for category in categories %}
                    {% for subcategory in category.subcategories %}
                        <div class="i-fld"><label><input type="radio" name="subcategory" value="{{ subcategory.slug }}"
                            {{ chosen and chosen.slug == subcategory.slug ? 'checked' }}> {{ subcategory.path }}</label><span></span></div>
                    {% endfor %}
                {% endfor %}
            </div>
        </noscript>

        {# THE GATE. Steps 1 and 2 are required and step 3 is not, so the File
           control is dead — visually and functionally — until a category is
           chosen, one line says what happened and the place is marked. The quiet
           line names whatever is still missing instead of making anybody press a
           disabled button to find out.

           The SERVER refuses the same filing for the same three reasons
           ({@see IncidentReportController::create}); this only says so sooner,
           and the button ships disabled so a filer without JavaScript is never
           shown a control that would be refused. The noscript block below hands
           it back, because without the controller nothing can enable it. #}
        <div class="i-sheetfoot">
            {# The gate REPLACES the reassuring line rather than crowding in
               beside it: both are the same quiet mono note in the same place,
               and only one of them is worth reading at a time. The hint ships
               hidden and the gate ships showing, because on a fresh form there
               is always something missing. #}
            <span class="hint" {{ stimulus_target(controller, 'hint') }} hidden>Nothing is written until you file. A filed
                incident starts at <b class="acc">reported</b> and cannot skip verification.</span>
            <span class="i-gate" {{ stimulus_target(controller, 'gate') }}>choose a category · describe what happened</span>
            <span class="sp"></span>
            {% if not standalone %}<button class="tgl" type="button" {{ stimulus_action(controller, 'close') }}>Cancel</button>{% endif %}
            <button class="cta" type="submit" {{ stimulus_target(controller, 'file') }} disabled>File incident →</button>
        </div>
        <noscript>
            <div class="i-sheetfoot">
                <span class="hint">Choose a kind above, say what happened and give the place — the report is refused
                    without all three.</span>
                <span class="sp"></span>
                <button class="cta" type="submit">File incident →</button>
            </div>
        </noscript>
    </form>
</div>
